===========================================================================
$NetBSD$

Akvorado requires Kafka and ClickHouse, which are not installed by this
package. Review the Kafka and ClickHouse addresses in
${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/akvorado.yaml before starting the services.

The sample configuration runs every service on a single host, each with
its own HTTP port:

	orchestrator  :8080  (configuration served to the other services)
	inlet         :8081  (flows on UDP 2055 NetFlow, 4739 IPFIX, 6343 sFlow)
	outlet        :8082  (BMP on TCP 10179)
	console       :8083  (web interface)

SO_REUSEPORT does not load-balance UDP flows on NetBSD, so the inlet uses
one worker per listening port.

Copy the rc.d scripts from ${PREFIX}/share/examples/rc.d (or set
PKG_RCD_SCRIPTS=YES) and enable the services in /etc/rc.conf. Start Kafka
and ClickHouse first: the orchestrator exits when they are unreachable, and
the other services exit when the orchestrator is unreachable. Logs are
written to ${VARBASE}/log/akvorado.
===========================================================================
